---
/** About / Origin — Figma 146:332, 1440 × 729. */
import Lines from '../Lines.astro';
---

<section class="about-origin padding-global padding-section-large" data-reveal-section>
  <div class="container-large about-origin_inner">
    <div class="about-origin_block" data-reveal-group>
      <Lines class="text-style-tagline text-color-sandy-brown" lines={['Our ground']} />
      <div class="about-origin_row">
        <Lines tag="h2" class="heading-style-h1" lines={['Textile knowledge', 'belongs to the place.']} />
        <p class="text-size-large about-origin_body" data-reveal>
          Crestloom begins in Panipat, where textiles are not treated as a trend or an abstraction. They are part of the city’s working rhythm—understood through materials, making, and the practical decisions behind every finished piece.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-origin_rule" role="presentation" data-reveal></div>

    <div class="about-origin_row" data-reveal-group>
      <Lines tag="p" class="heading-style-h2 about-origin_statement" lines={['The company is new.', 'The understanding behind it is not.']} />
      <p class="text-size-large about-origin_body" data-reveal>
        Our perspective is informed by a family familiar with textile manufacturing and the realities behind production. Crestloom brings that knowledge into a clearer, more considered sourcing partnership.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .about-origin { background-color: var(--color--offwhite); }
  .about-origin_inner {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 5rem;                        /* 80 */
  }
  .about-origin_block {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: 2rem;                        /* 32 */
  }
  .about-origin_row {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
  }
  .about-origin_body { width: 33.125rem; }        /* 530 */
  .about-origin_statement { width: 34.0625rem; }  /* 545 */
  .about-origin_rule {
    height: 1px;
    background-color: var(--color--text);
  }
</style>
